WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.033
Your blueprint ended with
a list of what it requires.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:06.133
Plug in what you already use,
and GTM OS reads your CRM,

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.900
your search data and your enrichment.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.233
Then it tells you exactly
what's still missing.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.233
In this clip you'll connect looot, your
CRM, search data and a mail sender.

00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:16.700
Then you'll read one strip
that shows which are live.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:19.867
Without it, Leo pastes keys
into six tool consoles.

00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:22.600
One key expires, an
enrichment call fails quietly,

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.100
and nobody notices until
Mia's numbers look wrong.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.633
Here's the rule. A few core
connections are native,

00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:30.000
and everything else goes
through Composio or looot.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.733
Secrets are sealed under
your master key, shown once,

00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:33.900
and never pass through a prompt.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.133
A connection you add for
your organization wins

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.933
over a key set for the whole instance.

00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:39.667
That keeps one record of what is live.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:42.833
A bad key shows up as a line,
not a quiet gap in Mia's numbers.

00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:44.567
Step one, the Connections page.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.533
In the console: Integrations,
then Connections.

00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:48.300
You get a grid of logos
grouped by category.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.067
Press the slash key to search by
name or category. Then sort the grid.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.200
Relevance to my setup is
the default, and it's real:

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.167
a tile ranks first when your
readiness says you need it,

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.867
with a reason like Needed by Outreach.

00:00:58.867 --> 00:01:01.133
You can also sort A to
Z, or Connected first.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.567
Or ask your agent: "What connections
do I need, and what is missing".

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.433
It reads the same readiness the grid uses,

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.767
and lists what's required and not yet
live. Reading is all it does here,

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:13.533
because entering a key or clicking an
OAuth consent is always your click.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:14.633
Step two, looot.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:18.000
It's the data provider built into GTM
OS: find and verify emails and phones,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.433
enrich a company or a
person, search the web,

00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:24.133
pull keyword and AI answer data.
You pay with one prepaid key,

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:25.767
under a small per call
cap that your admin sets.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:28.767
Anything above the cap
needs a person to approve.

00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:31.133
In the console: Connections,
looot, then paste your key.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.733
Connecting once for your
organization is enough,

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:35.867
because lookups run on
your organization's key

00:01:35.867 --> 00:01:37.733
and the instance key is only a fallback.

00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:40.333
Or ask your agent: "Quote
enriching these fifty accounts".

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.867
You get a price, not a charge.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:42.933
Here's the mechanism.

00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:45.867
If a provider has an outage, times
out or returns a server error,

00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:48.733
the next provider in the binding is
tried. Every attempt is recorded.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:51.133
That can mean two providers
were asked for one lookup,

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.400
and the attempt log says so.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.767
Step three, your own
apps, through Composio.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:58.267
In the console: Connections,
Composio, then Connect Composio.

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.100
Connect each app until it shows active.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.467
Pick your CRM of record: HubSpot,
Pipedrive, Zoho, Attio, or Salesforce,

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.833
which also goes through Composio.

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:08.867
Where a tile offers native
or via Composio, you choose.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.500
Or ask your agent: "Connect
HubSpot through Composio.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.333
Then sync HubSpot and show completeness".

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.833
It hands you a link, because
the sign in is yours.

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:17.633
Write backs to your CRM stay proposals,

00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:20.367
and a high risk write needs
one approval per record.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.133
Step four, search and analytics.
Ahrefs comes through Composio.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:26.400
Search Console and GA4 connect
in the console under Settings,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.267
then Connected accounts, with a
Google sign in, or through Composio.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:32.500
Search Console is required for
SEO and GEO, and only there.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.767
Connect it early, because it
keeps only months of history.

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:38.600
Or ask your agent: "Is Search Console
connected, and which property".

00:02:38.633 --> 00:02:42.333
Step five, a sender. The preferred
route is a Gmail or Microsoft mailbox,

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:45.333
ticked for sending under Connected
accounts. Resend works too.

00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:47.933
Smartlead, Instantly and lemlist
connect through Composio,

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:50.933
not as native cards. Connecting
a sender sends nothing,

00:02:50.933 --> 00:02:54.233
because Dry Mode stays on and
every send is still a logged draft.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.600
Step six, check your work.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:59.300
At the top of Connections, the Needed
strip lists what your setup requires,

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.067
one row each.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:04.233
Every connection reads live, unverified,
failed, fixture or not configured.

00:03:04.233 --> 00:03:07.700
Unverified means a key is saved but
never checked, so choose Test now.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.500
A failed row shows the
reason from the last check.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.733
An owner or admin can test, and
so can an agent acting for one.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.567
In the terminal: gtm doctor shows
the same lines. Advanced move:

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.333
gtm doctor with the strict flag exits

00:03:19.333 --> 00:03:21.333
with one when anything
you need isn't live,

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.100
so wire it into your scripts.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.733
Or ask your agent: "Test my connections
and tell me which ones fail".

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:27.733
One thing to watch.

00:03:27.733 --> 00:03:29.633
A fixture line means a built in sample

00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:31.800
response is standing
in for a real service.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.033
Demo mode says so, and sample data
never counts toward your first win.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:38.433
Neither does a model key or a sender
key. Only a real data source does.

00:03:38.433 --> 00:03:41.567
In live mode, a missing key
fails with the exact key to set.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.033
Real, or a dash with a
reason. Never a guess.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.467
Mia signs in to each app.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:48.200
Leo pastes the keys and sets
the Search Console property.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.667
Either way, the strip
tells you when you're done.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.900
The skeptic's line: a wall of logos
means that many native integrations.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.100
It doesn't. A few core
connections are native.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.200
The rest run through Composio,
and each tile says which,

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.167
so nothing claims more than it is.

00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:05.300
In one pass: Plug in looot,
your apps through Composio,

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.600
search data and a sender.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.667
Then read the Needed strip:
live, or a dash with a reason.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.267
You now have a CRM, a data
provider and search data connected,

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.500
and a line by line check of what is live.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.800
Coming next: skills, the playbooks
your agent already knows.
